# Copy to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile on the VPS (after `apt install caddy`), replace
# the domain, then `systemctl reload caddy`. Caddy handles TLS certificate
# issuance/renewal automatically via Let's Encrypt — no certbot, no manual
# cert management.
#
# This assumes docker-compose.prod.yml's `app` service is bound to
# 127.0.0.1:3000 (as written) — Caddy runs on the host (not in Docker) and
# proxies straight to it.

api.your-domain.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000
}
